## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

**10 tests — 6 Critical findings, 1 Medium** | This suite is a textbook **coverage-touching** test class. Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called, but almost nothing is verified. This explains the 95% coverage + production bugs paradox perfectly.

---

### 🔴 Critical

#### 1. Systematic Coverage-Touching (entire file)

The suite methodically calls every public method on `ProductCatalog` in declaration order with no or trivial assertions. **6 of 10 tests have zero assertions; the other 4 use only `Assert.IsNotNull`**, which merely proves the method returned *something*.

#### 2. No Assertions — `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)

Calls `AddProduct` but never verifies the product was stored.

```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
```

#### 3. No Assertions — `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32)

Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the price changed.

```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated?.Price);
```

#### 4. No Assertions — `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38)

Calls `RemoveProduct` but never checks the product is gone.

```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

#### 5. No Assertions — `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)

Captures nothing; doesn't even assign the return value to verify.

```csharp
// FIX:
var count = _catalog.GetProductCount();
Assert.AreEqual(0, count);
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(1, _catalog.GetProductCount());
```

#### 6. No Assertions — `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)

Applies a 10% discount to two products but never verifies prices changed.

```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")?.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")?.Price);
```

#### 7. No Assertions — `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 85)

Imports CSV but never verifies the product was created.

```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var imported = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
